  "operation_ledger_version": 2,
  "scope": "Exact existing-surface evidence fallback: the preserved source inventory contains 34 official-survey operation entries, exactly matching the immutable count. Shared executable bindings for the same provider method/path are merged into one normalized endpoint. The cited official html_reference artifact is retained as the v2 provenance root; no operation was inferred from a documentation crawl. Prior source-surface scope: Pass B full-surface expansion: 6 read streams (lists, campaigns, list_contacts plus the wave2 3-stream base; list_tags and campaign_summary_reports new this pass, the latter a fan_out stream over every campaign id) and 13 write actions covering list/contact/tag/custom-field lifecycle plus automation enrollment. This IS the full documented v1.6 surface — v1.6 is EmailOctopus's legacy API version (v2 exists and is recommended for new integrations per the docs banner, but this connector targets v1.6 per its existing base_url/spec, and Pass B stays within that version rather than silently migrating to a different API version). Excluded: the per-recipient campaign engagement-detail reports (bounced/clicked/complained/opened/sent/unsubscribed/not-clicked/not-opened contact lists — a large per-recipient analytics breakdown distinct from the aggregate summary report), the bulk multi-contact update endpoint, and single-object detail-by-id endpoints that duplicate an already-covered list stream's record shape.",
